  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed single storey side extension, by reason of its combination of positioning along the border, and its height and depth would result in material harm to neighbouring amenity due to an increase sense of enclosure and impact on light to neighbouring Flat 1, 53 Latimer Road, contrary to Local Plan policies D12.3 (Ensuring high quality design for all developments) and D12.4  (Alterations and extensions to existing buildings). ",
    "Reason : 2 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tThe applicant/agent was informed of any issues arising during consideration of the application and how these could potentially be overcome but sufficient information was not forthcoming. \r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\"\tThe applicant is advised to seek pre-application advice on any resubmission.\r\n"
  ],
